Subject: Cantor Bounded Candidate Mutation Exploded Specification

@ [source] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-30_cantor_bounded_candidate_mutation\Cantor_Phase3B_Bounded_Candidate_Mutation_Source_Selection.sop
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Bounded_Candidate_Mutation.sop
@ [research] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Codex_Workspace_Write_Boundary_Assessment_2026-07-30.sop

& [SubjectAxis] is one mutation run
  + [entry] is exact Phase3A request and fresh receipt
  + [worker] is one pinned Codex App Server child, one ephemeral thread, and one turn
  + [target] is one disposable candidate linked worktree
  + [exit] is handoff pending seal or quarantine

& [AuthorityAxis] is deliberately incomplete
  + [inside] is local candidate filesystem mutation and evidence capture
  + [outside] is preparation, principal or Git-common-dir write, network, credentials, approvals, authoritative sealing, acceptance, cleanup, repository history, and promotion
  + [current_signature] authorizes formation only
  - never: launch a writer under the formation signature

& [PreventionAxis] is physical
  + [sandbox] is workspaceWrite with no network, no additional roots, and excluded temp
  + [root] is exact canonical candidate cwd
  + [setup] rejects world-writable and failed Windows sandbox scans
  + [proof_matrix] challenges principal, common dir, parent, temp, network, symlink, reparse, hardlink, alias, and allowed path
  + [nonclaim] is stable schema describes policy but does not prove target-host enforcement

& [DetectionAxis] is reactive
  + [command_event] arrives as evidence with a best-effort action parse
  + [file_change_event] arrives as provisional path and diff evidence
  + [interrupt] limits continuation after a fault
  + [quarantine] preserves possible partial mutation
  + [post_state] is deferred to Phase3C
  - never: describe detection or interruption as transactional prevention

& [ProtocolAxis] is strict
  + [startup] is initialize, initialized, thread start, returned-authority check, and sandbox-ready notifications
  + [turn] is exact workspaceWrite policy, one input, closed output schema, and no approvals
  + [items] are commandExecution, fileChange, exact Cantor MCP, final agent message, and bounded advisory reasoning
  + [terminal] is exact correlated completion or typed fault
  + [forbidden] is unknown item, server request, dynamic tool, standalone command, steering, retry, and persistence

& [CommandAxis] is evidence-first
  + [identity] is item, command bytes, cwd, source, lifecycle, output, exit, duration, and process
  + [cwd] stays inside canonical candidate
  + [model_test] is not proof
  + [Git_history] and [network] and [credential] signals fault and quarantine
  + [ambiguity] is never resolved in favor of authority

& [FileAxis] is provisional until sealed
  + [event_path] is normalized, candidate-contained, and compared to allowlist
  + [event_diff] is bounded but not authoritative state
  + [rename_delete] needs explicit permission
  + [special_file] is forbidden
  + [outside_policy] causes interrupt and quarantine

& [DataAxis] is proof carrying
  + [MutationWorkPacket] binds entry, purpose, policy, counsel, criteria, and budgets
  + [MutationEvent] binds ordered physical observations
  + [MutationRunRecord] binds admission, Codex identity, sandbox, events, report, resources, and terminal state
  + [MutationFault] binds class, operation, evidence prefix, may-have-mutated, and quarantine
  + [Phase3CHandoff] binds physical state without accepting it

& [LifecycleAxis] is Prepared to Revalidated to SandboxReady to TurnRunning to TurnTerminal to HandoffPendingSeal to Closed
  + [fault_transition] after turn start goes to Quarantined then Closed
  + [fault_transition] before turn start goes directly to Closed
  + [retry] is absent
  + [reuse] is absent
  + [cleanup] is absent

& [FaultAxis] is consequence aware
  + [prestart] may truthfully report no model mutation
  + [poststart] reports mutation true or unknown
  + [interrupt_failure] does not suppress cleanup or evidence
  + [process_failure] preserves exact-child ownership
  + [sealer_unavailable] quarantines rather than accepting

& [VerificationAxis] precedes activation
  + [fake_protocol] proves every event, request, identity, budget, and lifecycle fault
  + [physical_sandbox] proves allowed and denied write targets on the target OS
  + [canary_files] make every escape attempt measurable without risking user data
  + [no_write_dry_run] proves admission and setup before the first live mutation
  + [one_write_probe] requires a disposable synthetic repository and separately renewed authority
  + [global] preserves all prior tests, docs, audit, evidence, and rollback
